# OAuth Role Selection Patterns

## OAuth Authentication Flow

OAuth users (Google, and future providers) must select their role on first sign-in.

### Flow Overview

1. User clicks "Sign in with Google"
2. OAuth authentication completes
3. New user created with `profileComplete: false`
4. User redirected to `/profile-setup`
5. [OAuthRoleSelection](mdc:src/app/components/auth/OAuthRoleSelection.tsx) component displays
6. User selects Attorney or Client role
7. Profile marked as complete
8. User redirected to dashboard

## OAuth Handler Configuration

In [src/lib/auth.ts](mdc:src/lib/auth.ts):

```typescript
async signIn({ user, account, profile }) {
  if (account?.provider === 'google') {
    const existingUser = await prisma.user.findUnique({
      where: { email: user.email! }
    })

    if (!existingUser) {
      // Create new OAuth user - force role selection
      await prisma.user.create({
        data: {
          name: user.name,
          email: user.email,
          emailVerified: new Date(),
          role: 'CUSTOMER', // Default role
          profileComplete: false, // Forces role selection
          accounts: { create: { /* account data */ } }
        }
      })
    }
  }
  return true
}
```

## Role Selection Component

Use [OAuthRoleSelection](mdc:src/app/components/auth/OAuthRoleSelection.tsx) for role selection:

```typescript
import { OAuthRoleSelection } from '@/app/components/auth/OAuthRoleSelection'

function ProfileSetup() {
  const [showRoleSelection, setShowRoleSelection] = useState(false)
  
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!session?.user?.profileComplete) {
      setShowRoleSelection(true)
    }
  }, [session])
  
  if (showRoleSelection) {
    return <OAuthRoleSelection onComplete={() => router.push('/')} />
  }
}
```

## Role Selection UI

The OAuthRoleSelection component provides:
- Visual role cards (Attorney/Client)
- Role descriptions and features
- Confirmation before submission
- Error handling
- Loading states

